spec_review_ok: GA-012 in DESIGN.md match their records, no open contradictions; 2 open ambiguities, not blocking:
  GA-012 A1 (GA-012.1, GA-012.2): GA-012.1 returns `closed` whenever `coverage_exception` holds words. It also says an exception passed with checked coverage 'isn't recorded and changes nothing.' Is the filter applied in `release`, so the handoff never carries the exception, or inside `lane_in_force`? What does `lane_in_force` return when called with words and checked coverage?
  GA-012 A2 (GA-012.3, GA-012.4, Coverage is mandatory): Is `human_merge_recorded` for an exception handoff limited to the Release Owner's own login, or does a merge by any other human count? The plan says 'the Release Owner', 'the owner' and 'a human merge' without defining the identity check.
